---
description: Provider adapter and integration rules
alwaysApply: true
---
Domain models are provider independent. Talk to vendors only through Vector adapters.
Required adapter families: AIProvider, EmailProvider, SocialProvider, AnalyticsProvider, StorageProvider, SearchProvider. SearchProvider may include official Search Console / Bing sync and optional generative-visibility measurement that can return unsupported. Do not invent extra search adapter families. Image and video work adds ImageProvider and later VideoProvider / ImageTransformProvider. Outcomes work adds CRMProvider (memory default; no vendor adapter) and may later add RevenueProvider, AdProvider, and BillingProvider. Do not add generateImage to AIProvider. Do not invent a second object-store adapter. Do not couple the domain to one CRM, ad network, or payment processor. Do not scrape restricted consumer AI interfaces for GEO measurement.
Grok is the first AI implementation, not a hard-coded dependency throughout the domain.
Use official provider APIs. Do not drive production publishing through browser automation.
Encrypt provider tokens at rest. Never send them to the browser, logs, or the model.
Every adapter needs typed IO, timeout, retry, idempotency, normalized errors, health, audit, and metrics.
Webhooks verify signatures, deduplicate event IDs, ack quickly, and finish work in durable jobs.
